      text: 'Participants were put in a romantic frame of mind, by looking at photos of attractive people and imagining an ideal first date, or in a neutral one. Then they said how they would spend their time and money. Romantically primed men planned more conspicuous spending and more heroic, risky helping. Romantically primed women offered more volunteering, but only where it would be seen; private helping did not rise. Desire, the study suggests, makes people generous in exactly the ways that can be noticed.',
