      title: 'Airport separations: a naturalistic study of adult attachment dynamics in separating couples',
      text: 'Couples in a public airport, some about to be parted by a flight and some travelling together, each filled in a short questionnaire about attachment style and how distressed they felt. Then observers quietly watched them. Relationship length and whether a couple was parting shaped how much they clung to each other. Anxious women felt more distress before a goodbye; avoidant women sought less contact, gave less comfort and looked away. A goodbye at the gate, the authors concluded, organises adult attachment much as a parent’s leaving organises a child’s.',
