    scenario: 'On their third date he asks about her childhood and listens for an hour: the busy parents, the boarding school, the birthdays nobody remembered. Two weeks later he turns up with a cake on an ordinary Tuesday, insists she wear a scarf and gently tells her off for skipping lunch. She hears herself giggling like a little girl and finds she can’t stay away.',
