    shadow: 'The thrill of crossing lines escalates. Each limit, once broken, loses its charge, so the next has to be further out, and some lines exist to protect people. Secrecy cuts the target off from the friends who might warn them, which is why abusers and groomers use the same language of a special, forbidden understanding, above all with the young. Shared guilt can become a hold: what you did together is what they can expose. And as Abelard and Heloise discovered, the people whose trust was broken do not always forgive.',
    honest: 'Exploring what you were taught to be ashamed of can be freeing, with a partner who treats your limits as yours to move, at your own pace, with clear agreement at every step and the freedom to stop at any point.',
