    shadow: 'Spiritual language is a powerful disguise, and the people most moved by it are often the most sincere and the most vulnerable. Gurus, cult leaders and abusive clergy have long used it to turn sexual demands into sacred duties, so that saying no feels like a failure of faith. When Beecher’s affair came out, he kept his pulpit; the parishioner who had trusted him lost her marriage and her church. Even in ordinary romances, talk of destiny makes it harder to leave: if the love was written in the stars, every warning sign becomes a test to endure.',
    honest: 'Shared wonder is one of the best things two people can have. Bring your real loves, whether music, faith, nature or ideas, into a relationship and let them deepen it. Just don’t claim a destiny you can’t know, and never use the sacred to ask for what you couldn’t ask for plainly.',
